@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-use-rfc-7386-merge-semantics
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use RFC 7386 merge semantics"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients submit JSON Merge Patch documents and need RFC 7386 behaviour alongside
+the existing RFC 6901 and RFC 6902 APIs. The public API must continue to accept
+only JSON values and must not mutate either supplied value.
+
+## Decision
+
+Expose `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`. Validate both arguments as JSON values,
+then apply RFC 7386 recursively: an object patch merges its own properties into
+an object target, `null` removes an object member, and every non-object patch
+replaces the target. Return independently cloned JSON containers.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Merge patches can replace any target value, including the document root and
+arrays. A `null` patch at the root returns `null`, whereas `null` members of an
+object patch remove those members. Callers receive a result without mutable
+container aliases to the target or patch.
