+---
+id: task-004-implement-json-merge-patch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Merge Patch"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Implement RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch and export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)`
+from `src/index.ts`.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Implemented recursive object merging, null-member deletion, whole-value
+  replacement for non-object patches, and conversion of non-object targets to
+  objects when applying an object patch.
+- Reused JSON validation, structural cloning, and safe own-property definition.
+  Neither input is mutated, and returned containers share no mutable aliases
+  with either input. Prototype-related names remain ordinary JSON properties.
+- Documented the public API, examples, input requirements, and null semantics
+  in README.md and the exported function's doc comment.
+- Followed approved decision `dl-004-use-rfc-7386-merge-semantics`.
+
+## Acceptance and verification
+
+All acceptance criteria for the new API were classified as red-first: RFC
+semantics, input independence, special property names, null-prototype objects,
+and rejection of non-JSON inputs. Added tests before implementation and
+confirmed `npm test` failed because the requested export did not exist. Existing
+JSON Pointer and JSON Patch tests served as characterization checks and passed.
+
+After implementation, `npm test` compiled TypeScript and passed all 30 tests,
+including all 15 RFC 7386 Appendix A examples and the new edge/error cases.
+`git diff --check` also passed. No dependencies were added.
